   "review_text": "This place is my go to for relaxation after work on on the weekend. Best food and drink selection. All the employees are very friendly and the owner Alfredo is a gem."
  },

{
   "review_stars": 3.0,
   "review_date": "2014-07-27 01:04:09",
   "review_text": "This is a local dive and popular around happy hour. They have awesome margaritas and decent seating outside. The staff is always pleasant. The food is another story. Since we usually just go for drinks and chips (good salsa) I can only speak for today's dinner. The food is expensive. $16 for a tostada. We decided to split it. The staff split it in the back and brought it to us on two plates (again, the staff is great). The quality?  Not good. I thought for sure it was canned chicken, the beans definitely right out of a can. There was nothing to substantiate a $16 meal. I would have complained if it was $5 cuz flat out it wasn't good. They refunded us the $16 for food and we happily paid the $36 for drinks. Go for the drinks and target the days when they serve free appetizers during happy hour. You'll never be disappointed."
  }
 ]
}

